                <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

                <h3>Will BC get more nominations later in 2026?</h3>
                <p>
                    Yes. On August 18, 2026, IRCC added 1,000 nominations,
                    raising BC's 2026 allocation from 5,254 to 6,254. In 2025,
                    BC's allocation also rose mid-year, from 4,000 to 6,214.
                </p>

                <h3>Should I still apply if numbers are low?</h3>
                <p>
                    Yes! Competition will be higher, but qualified candidates
                    will still receive invitations. Focus on maximizing your
                    score and targeting priority occupations.
                </p>

                <h3>When will student streams reopen?</h3>
                <p>
                    They will not. On April 23, 2026, BC said it will not launch
                    new student streams. Graduates can still earn education points
                    in Skills Immigration with a qualifying job offer.
                </p>

                <h3>How many draws will there be in 2026?</h3>
                <p>
                    Fewer than we expected in January. From February 4 to October
                    29, 2026, WelcomeBC published Skills Immigration rounds on 18
                    dates, issuing at least 7,085 invitations by our count. Since May,
                    the pattern has been roughly one Care and Build round and one
                    Innovate round a month. See our <a href="/articles/bc-pnp-2026-draws-recap-2027-forecast">2026 draws recap</a>.
                </p>
